## 27. Security Checklist

*   [ ] **SSL/TLS Encryption:** Force HTTPS on all frontend and backend endpoints. Terminate SSL at the edge gateway/load balancer.
*   [ ] **Password Hashing:** Ensure all passwords are encrypted with `BCryptPasswordEncoder` using a strength/rounds setting of 10-12.
*   [ ] **Method-Level Protection:** Ensure all administrative and instructor endpoints are protected on the backend using `@PreAuthorize("hasRole('...')")` rather than relying on frontend routing locks.
*   [ ] **SQL Injection Prevention:** Avoid writing raw SQL queries. Utilize Spring Data JPA repository method signatures or parameter binding in `@Query` to prevent SQL injection.
*   [ ] **XSS Sanitization:** Sanitize all rich-text input from users and instructors before storing it in the database or rendering it in the frontend.

